<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Use the trapezoidal rule with <m>4</m> strips to estimate the area bounded by the curve <m>y = {x^2+3 x+2}</m>, the <m>x</m>-axis and the lines <m>x = {0}</m> and <m>x = {2}</m>. Give exact values.</p><p>(a) What is the strip width <m>h</m>?</p><div><m>h =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the ordinates <m>y_0</m> to <m>y_4</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y_0</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y_1</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y_2</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y_3</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y_4</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="6" name="o0"/></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="6" name="o1"/></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="6" name="o2"/></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="6" name="o3"/></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="6" name="o4"/></cell></row></tabular><div>     </div><p>(c) Estimate the area with the trapezoidal rule.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans7"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) <m>h = \dfrac{b - a}{n} = \dfrac{ {2} - {0} }{4} = {0.5}</m>.</p><p>(b) The ordinates are the heights at <m>x = {0}, {0.5}, \ldots, {2}</m>:</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3.75}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8.75}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(c) Each inner ordinate is a side of two trapezia, so it is counted twice:</p><p><me>A \approx \tfrac{1}{2} \times {0.5} \times \left[{2} + {12} + 2({3.75} + {6} + {8.75})\right] = {12.75}</me></p><p>The curve bends upwards on this interval, so the chords lie above it and this estimate is too big.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{2}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{15}{4}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>6</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{35}{4}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>12</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{51}{4}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>